    <bpmn:process id="W_W1175" name="W1175. Sustainable Packaging Reduction &amp; Single-Use Plastic Elimination Program" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual ESG sustainability target setting; or regulatory development (Philippine EPR law compliance); or vendor packaging review cycle
Frequency: Quarterly program review; monthly packaging metric tracking; annual target setting
Volume: 35,000 active SKUs with packaging; ~800–1,000 vendors supplying packaged goods; ~200 stores generating packaging waste
Owner: Sustainability Lead
Participants: Category Manager, Procurement, Vendor, Store Operations, Waste Management, ESG Manager, VP Merchandising
Source: workflow W1175 — Sustainable Packaging Reduction &amp; Single-Use Plastic Elimination Program</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1175_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1175_Lane1" name="Sustainability Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1175_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1175_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1175_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1175_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1175_Lane2" name="Procurement">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1175_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1175_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1175_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1175_Lane4" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1175_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1175_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1175_Start6" name="Annual ESG sustainability target setting; or regulatory development (Philippine EPR law…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1175_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1175_Task7" name="Packaging baseline assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Packaging baseline assessment: Sustainability Lead conducts annual packaging audit: (a) total packaging weight by material type (plastic, cardboard, styrofoam, mixed) across supply chain; (b) top-50 packaging generators by vendor; (c) customer bag usage (plastic vs. reusable vs. no bag); (d) packaging-to-product weight ratio by category; (e) current recycling/recovery rate per W193 waste management
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1175_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1175_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1175_Task8" name="Annual reduction targets">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Annual reduction targets: Set packaging reduction targets aligned with Philippine EPR law requirements: (a) plastic packaging reduction: 20% by Year 3 vs. baseline; (b) single-use plastic bag elimination at checkout by Year 2 (reusable bag program already per W193); (c) vendor packaging: require top-20 vendors to submit sustainable packaging plans; (d) internal packaging: reduce shrink wrap usage by 30% through alternative pallet stabilization; (e) targets approved by VP Merchandising and included in ESG report per W694
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead / VP Merchandising
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1175_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1175_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1175_Task9" name="Vendor packaging engagement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Vendor packaging engagement: Procurement engages vendors on packaging reduction: (a) include sustainable packaging criteria in vendor scorecard per W44; (b) require new vendors per W36 to provide packaging sustainability declaration; (c) for top-20 vendors by packaging volume: request packaging reduction roadmap with milestones; (d) evaluate vendor proposals for: minimal packaging, recyclable materials, returnable packaging per W785, concentrated product formats (less packaging per unit of product); (e) prioritize categories: cleaning chemicals (concentrated refills), hardware (eliminate blister packs for fasteners), paint (returnable containers)
Responsible (R): Procurement / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1175_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1175_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1175_Task10" name="Store-level packaging management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Store-level packaging management: Store Operations implements: (a) reusable bag program — sell branded BuildRight reusable bags at checkout; train cashiers to ask before bagging; track bag usage by store; (b) cardboard baling and recycling per W193 — all stores have cardboard balers; target 95% cardboard recovery; (c) vendor packaging return — negotiate with vendors to take back packaging materials (especially styrofoam and large boxes) during next delivery; (d) customer packaging return station — pilot collection point for clean packaging (plastic containers, cardboard) at store entrance for recycling
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1175_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1175_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1175_Task11" name="Monthly packaging metrics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Monthly packaging metrics: System tracks: (a) plastic bag usage per store (target: 50% reduction Year 1), (b) cardboard recovery rate by store, (c) vendor packaging compliance rate, (d) total packaging waste per PHP 1M revenue, (e) sustainable packaging adoption rate; monthly dashboard shared with Category Managers and Store Managers
Responsible (R): System / Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): ESG Manager
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1175_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1175_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1175_Task12" name="Quarterly program review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Quarterly program review: Sustainability Lead presents progress to ESG Committee: (a) actual vs. target for all packaging KPIs, (b) vendor engagement progress, (c) store compliance by region, (d) cost impact analysis (sustainable packaging may increase COGS by 1–3%), (e) regulatory compliance status (EPR law reporting), (f) recommendations for target adjustment or acceleration
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1175_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1175_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1175_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1175_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1175_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-316 (ensure controlled execution — Environmental Monitoring (PA-25.1).) | - operational: Sustainability Lead review and approval gate
Owner: Sustainability Lead</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1175_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1175_Annotation14" targetRef="W1175_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
