    <bpmn:process id="W_W1447" name="W1447. Store-Level Construction Material Pallet, Packaging &amp; Wooden Crate Recovery &amp; Supplier Return Program" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Weekly accumulation of pallets, wooden crates, and reusable packaging from inbound deliveries; or monthly pallet reconciliation cycle
Frequency: Weekly pallet/packaging collection per store; monthly reconciliation with suppliers; quarterly program performance review
Volume: ~15–20 pallets/week per store × 200 stores = ~3,000–4,000 pallets/week chain-wide; ~150,000–200,000 pallets/year; plus wooden crates (tiles), metal bands, and reusable packaging
Owner: Store Receiving Clerk / DC Logistics Coordinator
Participants: Receiving Clerk, Stock Associate, Department Supervisor, DC Logistics Coordinator, Vendor Logistics Contact, VP Supply Chain
Source: workflow W1447 — Store-Level Construction Material Pallet, Packaging &amp; Wooden Crate Recovery &amp; Supplier Return Program</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1447_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1447_Lane1" name="Receiving Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1447_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1447_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1447_Lane2" name="DC Logistics Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1447_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1447_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1447_Lane3" name="Finance Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1447_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1447_Lane4" name="VP Supply Chain">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1447_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1447_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1447_Start6" name="Weekly accumulation of pallets, wooden crates, and reusable packaging from inbound…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1447_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1447_Task7" name="Pallet and packaging sorting at receiving">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Pallet and packaging sorting at receiving: When inbound delivery is unloaded per W4: (a) Receiving Clerk sorts pallets and packaging into: (i) &quot;Return to Vendor&quot; — standard pallets in good condition, reusable crates, vendor-specific totes, (ii) &quot;Reuse In-Store&quot; — pallets usable for in-store display (e.g., lumber display pallets), (iii) &quot;Recycle/Scrap&quot; — broken pallets, damaged crates, non-reusable packaging, (b) tag returnable pallets with vendor ID using color-coded tags or barcode labels, (c) stack returnable pallets in designated backroom staging area (max 7-day accumulation)
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5 min per delivery</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1447_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1447_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1447_Task8" name="Weekly pallet return coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Weekly pallet return coordination: DC Logistics Coordinator manages weekly pallet return cycle: (a) system generates pallet return schedule based on: (i) accumulated pallet count by vendor at each store, (ii) vendor&#x27;s next scheduled delivery to the store or DC, (iii) pallet return threshold (minimum 20 pallets per vendor per pickup), (b) for vendor-direct pickup: coordinate with vendor logistics to pick up returnable pallets during next delivery run (backhaul), (c) for DC-consolidated return: stores return pallets to DC on empty outbound trucks; DC accumulates and ships bulk pallet returns to vendors monthly
Responsible (R): DC Logistics Coordinator
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 4 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1447_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1447_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1447_Task9" name="Monthly pallet reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Monthly pallet reconciliation: DC Logistics Coordinator reconciles pallet positions: (a) pallets received (from inbound deliveries) minus pallets returned (to vendors) minus pallets recycled should equal net pallet position, (b) investigate discrepancies: (i) unreturned pallets piling up at stores (storage issue), (ii) missing pallets (potential theft — wooden pallets have scrap value), (iii) damaged pallets not properly categorized, (c) vendor dispute resolution: if vendor claims fewer pallets returned than BuildRight records, investigate using delivery receipts and signed pallet return forms
Responsible (R): DC Logistics Coordinator
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1447_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1447_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1447_Task10" name="Pallet rebate tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Pallet rebate tracking: Finance tracks pallet return rebates: (a) vendors offering pallet return credits (typically PHP 50–100 per standard pallet): (i) track pallets returned per vendor per month, (ii) reconcile vendor credit notes against pallet return records, (iii) AP applies credits to vendor payments per W7, (b) report monthly pallet rebate revenue as offset to logistics costs
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1447_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1447_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1447_Task11" name="Quarterly program review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quarterly program review: VP Supply Chain and ESG Manager review: (a) pallet return rate (target: ≥ 60% of standard pallets returned to vendors), (b) waste reduction impact (pallets diverted from landfill), (c) cost savings (rebates + avoided disposal fees), (d) vendor participation rate, (e) program expansion: identify additional vendors and packaging types for inclusion
Responsible (R): VP Supply Chain / ESG Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1447_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1447_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1447_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1447_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1447_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-316 (ensure controlled execution — Environmental Monitoring (PA-25.1).) | - operational: Store Receiving Clerk / DC Logistics Coordinator review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Store Receiving Clerk / DC Logistics Coordinator</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1447_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1447_Annotation13" targetRef="W1447_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1447_Flow15" sourceRef="W1447_Start6" targetRef="W1447_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1447_Flow16" sourceRef="W1447_Task7" targetRef="W1447_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1447_Flow17" sourceRef="W1447_Task8" targetRef="W1447_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1447_Flow18" sourceRef="W1447_Task9" targetRef="W1447_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1447_Flow19" sourceRef="W1447_Task10" targetRef="W1447_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1447_Flow20" sourceRef="W1447_Task11" targetRef="W1447_End12" />
    </bpmn:process>
