    <bpmn:process id="W_W1529" name="W1529. Responsible Timber &amp; Wood Product Sourcing, Chain-of-Custody Verification &amp; DENR Compliance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarterly timber sourcing review; new timber vendor onboarding; DENR audit; customer/media inquiry about sustainable sourcing
Frequency: Quarterly sourcing reviews; per-vendor verification at onboarding; annual DENR compliance reporting
Volume: ~15–25 timber/wood product vendors supplying lumber, plywood, MDF, doors, mouldings — representing ~8–12% of COGS
Owner: Category Manager (Timber &amp; Wood)
Participants: Category Manager, Sourcing Manager, Quality Assurance Specialist, DENR (Department of Environment and Natural Resources), vendor representatives
Source: workflow W1529 — Responsible Timber &amp; Wood Product Sourcing, Chain-of-Custody Verification &amp; DENR Compliance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1529_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1529_Lane1" name="Sourcing Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1529_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1529_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1529_Lane2" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1529_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1529_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1529_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1529_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1529_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1529_Start4" name="Quarterly timber sourcing review; new timber vendor onboarding; DENR audit…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1529_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1529_Task5" name="Vendor onboarding — timber due diligence">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Vendor onboarding — timber due diligence: (a) for every new timber/wood vendor: Sourcing Manager collects: (i) DENR-issued Certificate of Registration as timber dealer/processor, (ii) current Timber License Agreement (TLA) or Integrated Forest Management Agreement (IFMA) showing legal harvest area, (iii) DENR transport permit (certificate of origin) for current batch, (iv) chain-of-custody documentation: harvest site → sawmill → vendor → BuildRight, (v) any third-party certification (FSC, PEFC, PHILGREEN); (b) Category Manager reviews documentation for: (i) validity (DENR permits have expiry dates), (ii) consistency (does the claimed harvest area match the species and volumes being sold?), (iii) gaps in chain-of-custody; (c) if documentation is incomplete: vendor cannot be onboarded until gaps are resolved
Responsible (R): Sourcing Manager / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 4–6 hours per new vendor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1529_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1529_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1529_Task6" name="Quarterly vendor documentation audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Quarterly vendor documentation audit: (a) Category Manager reviews all active timber vendors&#x27; documentation quarterly: (i) DENR permits renewed and current, (ii) chain-of-custody documents for recent shipments on file, (iii) no DENR enforcement actions or sanctions against vendor, (iv) FSC/PEFC certification status (if applicable — currently &lt; 30% of Philippine timber is certified); (b) flags vendors with: (i) expired permits (suspend purchasing until renewed), (ii) missing chain-of-custody for recent shipments (request retroactive documentation), (iii) known DENR enforcement (immediately suspend and investigate)
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2–3 days/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1529_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1529_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1529_Task7" name="DENR compliance reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: DENR compliance reporting: (a) annually: Category Manager compiles timber sourcing report for DENR: (i) total volume of wood products purchased (by species: lauan, apitong, yakal, tanguile, etc.), (ii) source documentation summary (vendors, permits, volumes), (iii) chain-of-custody audit results; (b) submits report to DENR Community Environment and Natural Resources Office (CENRO) if required by local regulation; (c) maintains 7-year documentation archive for DENR audit readiness
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2–3 days/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1529_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1529_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1529_Task8" name="Sustainable sourcing target management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Sustainable sourcing target management: (a) Category Manager tracks sustainable sourcing KPI: percentage of timber/wood products sourced from certified sustainable sources (FSC, PEFC, or DENR-verified legal + reforestation program); (b) annual target: increase certified sustainable sourcing by 5–10% per year (from current baseline of ~20–30% to target of 60% within 5 years); (c) actions to achieve target: (i) engage existing vendors on FSC/PEFC certification process (share cost, provide multi-year purchase commitment as incentive), (ii) source from vendors who participate in DENR&#x27;s National Greening Program (NGP), (iii) increase proportion of imported certified wood products (New Zealand pine, European spruce — higher cost but fully certified)
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1529_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1529_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1529_Task9" name="Customer communication and in-store messaging">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Customer communication and in-store messaging: (a) Marketing Communications Manager develops in-store signage for lumber section: (i) &quot;Responsible Wood Sourcing at BuildRight&quot; display with sustainability commitment, (ii) vendor certification status where applicable, (iii) QR code linking to BuildRight sustainability webpage; (b) if customer or media inquires about timber sourcing: Category Manager provides documented response with chain-of-custody evidence
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Marketing Comms Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising / VP Marketing
Duration: Initial setup: 2–3 days; ongoing: 1–2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1529_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1529_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1529_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1529_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1529_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-227 (ensure ESG data integrity &amp; disclosure.) | - operational: Category Manager (Timber &amp; Wood) review and approval gate
Owner: Category Manager (Timber &amp; Wood)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1529_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1529_Annotation11" targetRef="W1529_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1529_Flow13" sourceRef="W1529_Start4" targetRef="W1529_Task5" />
