    <bpmn:process id="W_W1530" name="W1530. Store-Level Rainwater Harvesting System, Green Infrastructure Initiative &amp; Sustainability Demonstration Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual sustainability initiative planning; new store construction (PA-20.2) incorporating green infrastructure; ESG reporting requirement (PA-25.3)
Frequency: Ongoing monitoring of installed systems; quarterly initiative review; annual expansion planning
Volume: Target: 50 stores with rainwater harvesting + 20 stores with additional green infrastructure (solar already covered per W1448) by Year 3
Owner: Facilities Engineer
Participants: Facilities Engineer, Store Manager, Sustainability Manager, Category Manager (Plumbing/Garden), ESG Reporting Analyst
Source: workflow W1530 — Store-Level Rainwater Harvesting System, Green Infrastructure Initiative &amp; Sustainability Demonstration Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1530_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1530_Lane1" name="Sustainability Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1530_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1530_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1530_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1530_Lane2" name="Facilities Engineer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1530_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1530_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1530_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1530_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1530_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1530_Start5" name="Annual sustainability initiative planning; new store construction (PA-20.2) incorporating…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1530_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1530_Task6" name="Green infrastructure assessment and planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Green infrastructure assessment and planning: (a) Sustainability Manager and Facilities Engineer assess each store for green infrastructure potential: (i) roof area and catchment potential (sqm × annual rainfall × collection efficiency of 80%), (ii) garden center water demand, (iii) toilet flushing demand (29 staff × 5 flushes/day × 6 liters/flush), (iv) exterior cleaning demand, (v) existing water source (municipal supply cost per cu.m.), (vi) space for water tank installation; (b) prioritize stores: highest ROI based on (i) highest municipal water cost, (ii) largest garden center water demand, (iii) highest rainfall area; (c) annual budget allocation: target 15–20 stores/year for rainwater harvesting installation (PHP 80K–150K per store for tank + gutter + filtration + plumbing)
Responsible (R): Sustainability Manager / Facilities Engineer
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 2–3 weeks/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1530_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1530_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1530_Task7" name="Installation coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Installation coordination (integrated with new store construction or retrofit): (a) for new stores (PA-20.2): Facilities Engineer includes rainwater harvesting and green infrastructure in construction specifications: (i) gutter system connected to water tank, (ii) first-flush diverter to discard initial roof runoff (debris/bird droppings), (iii) water tank (BuildRight&#x27;s own product — 2,000–5,000 liter polyethylene tank), (iv) filtration and pump system, (v) plumbing connection to garden center irrigation and staff restrooms; (b) for existing store retrofits: Facilities Engineer coordinates installation with store operations (schedule during low-traffic period, minimize disruption); (c) Category Manager (Plumbing) sources components from BuildRight&#x27;s own inventory (eat-your-own-cooking principle)
Responsible (R): Facilities Engineer / Construction Contractor
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 1–2 weeks installation per store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1530_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1530_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1530_Task8" name="Live product demonstration setup">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Live product demonstration setup: (a) in stores with rainwater harvesting: Store Manager sets up demonstration display near garden center: (i) transparent section of downpipe showing water flow, (ii) water level indicator on tank visible to customers, (iii) signage: &quot;This store captures and uses rainwater — reducing municipal water consumption by XX%. Ask us how to set up your own system!&quot;; (b) Category Manager (Plumbing/Garden) ensures related products are displayed nearby: water tanks, gutter systems, pumps, filtration units; (c) Project Estimator trained to reference store&#x27;s own system during W984 (Water Tank Sizing) consultations
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Category Manager
Accountable (A): Sustainability Manager
Duration: 1–2 days initial setup</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1530_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1530_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1530_Task9" name="Monthly monitoring and maintenance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Monthly monitoring and maintenance: (a) Facilities Engineer monitors installed systems: (i) monthly water capture volume (flow meter on tank inlet), (ii) monthly water consumption from tank (flow meter on tank outlet), (iii) system uptime (any days where rainwater was unavailable and municipal backup was used), (iv) maintenance issues (clogged gutters, pump failure, tank cleaning); (b) Store Manager or Maintenance Staff performs: (i) quarterly gutter cleaning, (ii) semi-annual tank inspection and cleaning, (iii) pump filter replacement per manufacturer schedule; (c) system data logged in sustainability dashboard
Responsible (R): Facilities Engineer / Store Maintenance Staff
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours/month per store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1530_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1530_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1530_Task10" name="ROI tracking and ESG reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: ROI tracking and ESG reporting: (a) quarterly: Sustainability Manager calculates ROI per system: (i) water cost savings (liters saved × municipal water rate), (ii) installation cost depreciation (straight-line over 10-year life), (iii) maintenance cost, (iv) net annual savings; (b) annually: ESG Reporting Analyst includes in sustainability report: (i) total rainwater harvested across all stores (liters), (ii) municipal water consumption reduction (%), (iii) number of stores with green infrastructure, (iv) product sales attribution (increased water tank/gutter/pump sales in stores with demo systems vs. without); (c) feeds into PA-25.3 ESG Reporting &amp; Compliance
Responsible (R): Sustainability Manager / ESG Reporting Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 4–6 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1530_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1530_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1530_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1530_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1530_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-316 (ensure controlled execution — Environmental Monitoring (PA-25.1).) | - operational: at PHP 80K–150K per store saves PHP 15K–30K/year in water costs
Owner: Facilities Engineer</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1530_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1530_Annotation12" targetRef="W1530_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1530_Flow14" sourceRef="W1530_Start5" targetRef="W1530_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1530_Flow15" sourceRef="W1530_Task6" targetRef="W1530_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1530_Flow16" sourceRef="W1530_Task7" targetRef="W1530_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1530_Flow17" sourceRef="W1530_Task8" targetRef="W1530_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1530_Flow18" sourceRef="W1530_Task9" targetRef="W1530_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1530_Flow19" sourceRef="W1530_Task10" targetRef="W1530_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1530_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1530_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1530">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1530_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1530_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1530_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1530_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1530_Lane3_di" bpmnElement="W1530_Lane3" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="420" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1530_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W1530_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1530_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W1530_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1530_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W1530_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="465" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1530_Task9_di" bpmnElement="W1530_Task9"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1530_Task10_di" bpmnElement="W1530_Task10"><dc:Bounds x="1240" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1530_Start5_di" bpmnElement="W1530_Start5"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1530_End11_di" bpmnElement="W1530_End11"><dc:Bounds x="1470" y="487" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1530_Annotation12_di" bpmnElement="W1530_Annotation12"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="630" width="360" height="60" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1530_Flow14_di" bpmnElement="W1530_Flow14"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1530_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W1530_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1530_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W1530_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="790" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="505" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1530_Flow17_di" bpmnElement="W1530_Flow17"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="505" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1530_Flow18_di" bpmnElement="W1530_Flow18"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="1240" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1530_Flow19_di" bpmnElement="W1530_Flow19"><di:waypoint x="1420" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1470" y="505" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1530_Assoc13_di" bpmnElement="W1530_Assoc13"><di:waypoint x="340" y="630" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1448" name="W1448. Store-Level Solar Panel Performance Monitoring, Energy Savings Tracking &amp; ROI Reporting" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly solar energy generation reporting cycle; or quarterly ROI review; or solar system fault alert
Frequency: Daily automated monitoring; monthly performance reporting; quarterly ROI review; ad-hoc fault response
Volume: ~80 stores with rooftop solar installations (one register with W173; target: all 200 stores over 5 years); each store system ~50–100 kW peak capacity
Owner: COO &amp; Construction (infrastructure) / Store Manager (daily)
Participants: Store Manager, COO, Facilities Engineer, Finance Controller, External Solar Provider (O&amp;M), ESG Manager
Source: workflow W1448 — Store-Level Solar Panel Performance Monitoring, Energy Savings Tracking &amp; ROI Reporting</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1448_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1448_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1448_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1448_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1448_Lane2" name="Facilities Engineer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1448_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1448_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1448_Lane3" name="Finance Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1448_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1448_Lane4" name="COO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1448_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1448_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1448_Start6" name="Monthly solar energy generation reporting cycle; or quarterly ROI review; or solar system…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1448_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1448_Task7" name="Daily automated monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Daily automated monitoring: Solar monitoring system tracks: (a) daily kWh generation per store, (b) system efficiency (actual generation vs. rated capacity × solar irradiance), (c) fault alerts: (i) inverter failure, (ii) panel degradation, (iii) grid disconnection, (iv) shading from new construction, (d) self-consumption ratio (kWh used in-store vs. kWh exported to grid), (e) Store Manager receives daily summary via mobile app; system auto-escalates faults to Facilities Engineer if generation drops &gt; 20% below expected
Responsible (R): System (automated)
Accountable (A): Facilities Engineer
Duration: Automated (Store Manager: 5 min/day review)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1448_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1448_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1448_Task8" name="Monthly performance reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Monthly performance reporting: Facilities Engineer compiles monthly solar performance report: (a) per-store: (i) total kWh generated, (ii) vs. expected generation (based on historical irradiance data), (iii) system uptime %, (iv) savings: kWh × blended electricity rate (PHP/kWh), (v) self-consumption vs. export and respective feed-in tariff revenue, (b) chain-wide: (i) total generation, (ii) total cost savings, (iii) CO₂ emissions avoided, (iv) system availability, (c) flag underperforming stores (&lt; 80% of expected generation) for maintenance investigation
Responsible (R): Facilities Engineer
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1448_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1448_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1448_Task9" name="Quarterly maintenance scheduling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Quarterly maintenance scheduling: Facilities Engineer coordinates with external solar O&amp;M provider: (a) quarterly panel cleaning (dust accumulation reduces efficiency by 10–15% in Philippine dry season), (b) annual inverter inspection, (c) annual panel thermal imaging scan (detect hot spots indicating cell degradation), (d) vegetation management (trim trees casting shadows on panels), (e) schedule maintenance during non-peak store hours to minimize disruption
Responsible (R): Facilities Engineer / External O&amp;M
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1448_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1448_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1448_Task10" name="Quarterly ROI tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quarterly ROI tracking: Finance Controller calculates solar investment ROI: (a) cumulative capital investment in solar installations, (b) cumulative energy savings and feed-in tariff revenue, (c) payback progress: cumulative savings ÷ investment, (d) IRR on solar investment, (e) compare actual savings vs. business case projections, (f) present to CFO and ESG Manager for sustainability reporting
Responsible (R): Finance Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1448_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1448_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1448_Task11" name="Annual expansion planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Annual expansion planning: COO and Finance Controller plan next year&#x27;s solar expansion: (a) identify stores scheduled for solar installation (prioritize high-electricity-cost locations), (b) evaluate new solar technology (higher efficiency panels, battery storage for nighttime use), (c) negotiate bulk pricing with solar provider for multi-store deployment, (d) include solar expansion in annual capex budget, (e) ESG Manager incorporates solar generation into annual sustainability report per W253
Responsible (R): COO / Finance Controller
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 1 week/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1448_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1448_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1448_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1448_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
