    <bpmn:process id="W_W1543" name="W1543. Utility Data Collection &amp; Store-Level Energy Consumption Monitoring" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly utility bill receipt; or consumption-anomaly alert; or quarterly carbon reporting cycle
Frequency: Monthly data collection; continuous consumption monitoring
Volume: 200 stores + 4 DCs + 1 HQ = 205 locations monitored
Owner: ESG Manager
Participants: ESG Manager, Store Managers, DC Managers, Facilities Manager, CFO
Source: workflow W1543 — Utility Data Collection &amp; Store-Level Energy Consumption Monitoring</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1543_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1543_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1543_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1543_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1543_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1543_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1543_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1543_Lane2" name="ESG Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1543_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1543_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1543_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1543_Start4" name="Monthly utility bill receipt; or consumption-anomaly alert; or quarterly carbon reporting…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1543_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1543_Task5" name="Utility data collection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Utility data collection: System automatically imports monthly electricity bills from utility company portals (Meralco, Davao Light, VECO, etc.) via API or manual entry by Store Manager; captures kWh consumption, peak demand (kW), and cost; diesel generator fuel consumption logged separately; water consumption tracked where metered
Responsible (R): System / Store Manager
Accountable (A): ESG Manager
Duration: 2 hours/month (manual entries)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1543_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1543_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1543_Task6" name="Energy intensity benchmarking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Energy intensity benchmarking: System calculates energy intensity per location — kWh per sqm per month; benchmarks stores against peer group (same format size, same climate zone, same operating hours); flags stores with energy intensity &gt; 20% above peer group average for investigation
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): ESG Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1543_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1543_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1543_Task7" name="Feed to carbon accounting (W1396)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Feed to carbon accounting (W1396): validated consumption data (electricity, diesel, LPG, water) flows monthly to W1396 (PA-25.3), which owns the annual Scope 1+2 carbon footprint estimation, the Philippine grid-emission-factor maintenance and the W198 fleet-emissions addition
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): ESG Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1543_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1543_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1543_Task8" name="Target-status monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Target-status monitoring: the Green/Amber/Red location status vs annual carbon and energy reduction targets is computed per W1396 (step 5); this workflow surfaces the dashboards and alert flags for location owners
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): ESG Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1543_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1543_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1543_Task9" name="Efficiency-lead hand-off">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Efficiency-lead hand-off: flagged high-consumption locations and identified root causes (aging HVAC, inefficient lighting, operational waste) route to the W1396 efficiency project pipeline (step 6) for ROI analysis and the capex request (W21)
Responsible (R): ESG Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: ~4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1543_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1543_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1543_Task10" name="Annual ESG energy disclosure">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Annual ESG energy disclosure: ESG Manager compiles annual energy and carbon data for the ESG report per W1396 (PA-25.3) — total energy consumption, carbon footprint, YoY change, reduction target achievement, energy efficiency investments made, renewable energy contribution (solar from W173); data verified by Internal Audit (W341) before external disclosure
Responsible (R): ESG Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 16 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1543_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1543_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1543_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1543_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1543_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-316 (ensure controlled execution — Environmental Monitoring (PA-25.1).) | - operational: ESG Manager review and approval gate
Owner: ESG Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
